  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Urban Programme: a fair, inclusive and sustainable city - 2017-23: Semeando</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Urban programme aim is to contribute to an inclusive city through capacity strengthening and training of local grassroots housing rights&apos; and neighbourhood organisations in S&#xe3;o Paulo in order to improve the living conditions of homeless families and families living in precarious and unsecure housing reducing their vulnerability to social and environmental risks. The specific aim of the programme is to consolidate the capacity of partners to support local organisations to defend pro-poor urban policies, participate in spaces of decision-making and carry out community-level training and capacity building on housing and related rights, and to protect housing rights defenders from persecution. This is the 3rd cycle of the Urban Programme in S&#xe3;o Paulo. The expected results are for Semeando (1) Capacity of 45 local organisations to accompany constituents to monitor and participate in urban planning processes, manage security risks related to their work, and protect the space to participate is built (2) Increased advocacy and networking capacity of housing groups to defend pro-poor urban policies (3) Public debate influenced through targeted and strategic communication with new and existing audiences (4) Increased institutional capacity of partners and local organisations.</narrative>
  </description>
